WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.590
Project time! Today you will analyse a monthly sales sheet with AI and prove every number is right.

2
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:13.610
Upload a CSV or Excel file to ChatGPT or Claude, or paste a few rows.

3
00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.890
Then ask what each column means and whether it sees any problems.

4
00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:22.430
A CSV is just a simple spreadsheet file that any tool can open.

5
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:29.330
Real sheets have duplicates, spelling differences like “bangalore” and “Bengaluru”, and blank cells.

6
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:34.680
Ask the AI to list problems, but fix them yourself so you know what changed.

7
00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.880
Messy data always gives you wrong totals, however clever the tool is.

8
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.530
Describe what you want and AI writes the formula.

9
00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:49.420
SUMIF adds up only the rows that match, like one region.

10
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:55.550
XLOOKUP or VLOOKUP finds a value from another table, and IF shows one thing or another, like “Target met”.

11
00:00:55.550 --> 00:01:01.800
Ask for a summary table by region or category, then make a chart in Excel or Google Sheets.

12
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:06.910
The golden rule: check every total with your own SUM before you share it.

13
00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:12.140
AI can miscount, especially when the data is messy or has duplicates.

14
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:17.670
ChatGPT and Claude can read a spreadsheet file and do the maths for you.

15
00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:23.330
First ask what each column means and what problems it sees, before any totals.

16
00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:28.870
Then always repeat the key totals in your own sheet, with your own formula.

17
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:34.250
Claude explains every column in plain words, then lists three problems.

18
00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:40.740
One invoice appears twice, one city is spelt two ways, and one row has blanks.

19
00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.550
These are exactly the problems that make totals go wrong.

20
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:49.380
You do not need to remember formulas, you just describe what you want.

21
00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:54.650
Gemini writes the SUMIF formula and explains it in one simple sentence.

22
00:01:54.650 --> 00:02:02.540
Type it into your sheet, and for West the answer is eighty-one thousand, nine hundred and thirty-five rupees.

23
00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:08.840
Now we ask ChatGPT for the month’s total, before cleaning the data.

24
00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:13.190
It says five lakh, forty-two thousand, six hundred and ninety-one rupees.

25
00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:18.110
But that counts the duplicate invoice twice, so the real total is lower.

26
00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:27.800
After cleaning, our own SUM gives five lakh, twenty-three thousand, nine hundred and seventy-one rupees.

27
00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:33.390
Some accounts have AI built right into Google Sheets or Excel, and some do not.

28
00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:39.950
If yours does not, simply ask a chatbot in another tab and paste the formula into your sheet.

29
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:43.130
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

30
00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:46.720
Now plan it, build it, test it, and share it!
